I cannot reproduce the same behavior as yours.

Here is the snippets I used.
```js
const fastify = require("fastify");

const app = fastify({ logger: true });
app.get('/:strangeId', (req, reply) => {
  reply.send({ strangeId: req.params.strangeId })
})

app.listen(3000);
```

Response.
```
{"error":"Bad Request","message":"'%c0' is not a valid url component","statusCode":400}
```

If your project is empty and not registered any route. Throwing `404` should be the correct behavior because it do not have a matching route for the URI params parsing. So, I will not consider it as a bug.
